WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.423
A bit represents one binary choice.

00:00:02.423 --> 00:00:04.442
Eight bits form a byte.

00:00:04.442 --> 00:00:11.306
Capacity calculations must keep bits, bytes and prefixes separate: decimal kilo means 1000, while kibi means 1024.

00:00:11.306 --> 00:00:18.170
A transfer rate in megabits per second cannot be compared directly with a file size in megabytes.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.477
There are 307,200 pixels.

00:00:21.477 --> 00:00:30.130
Multiplying by 24 gives 7,372,800 bits; dividing by 8 gives 921,600 bytes, or 900 KiB.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:36.475
The file on disk may differ because of headers or compression.

00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:39.815
How many bytes are in 64 bits?

00:00:39.815 --> 00:00:41.820
Divide the bit count by eight.
